  "version": 1,
  "notes": [
    "Keyed by ISO3 because that is what the trade panel already computes (countryCode() in app.js) before it asks the API for a country's reports.",
    "aliases are matched case-insensitively with word boundaries; cased_aliases are matched case-sensitively, for abbreviations that collide with ordinary words ('US' vs 'us', 'EU', 'UK', 'DRC').",
    "regions are subnational producing areas that imply the country on their own -- a WASDE line about Mato Grosso is a Brazil report even when it never writes 'Brazil'.",
    "Longest alias wins the span, so 'North Korea' beats 'Korea' and 'Papua New Guinea' beats 'Guinea'. Add new aliases without worrying about ordering."
